      "TEACHER CHARLIE: Are you done? What?\nCHARLIE: ...Almost.",
      "ANNIE: Charlie? Charlie shuts the box, SHOVES it into a corner, and peers down to see ANNIE at the tree’s base.\nANNIE: Come on, sweetie. It’s freezing out here. No response from Charlie. Annie doesn’t push it.\nANNIE: Okay, well, I’m running out for a sec. Is there anything I can bring you back?\nCHARLIE: Why??",
      "ANNIE: CHARLIE! Charlie looks to ANNIE, who is running in her direction. Charlie steps toward Annie.\nANNIE: What are you doing?! It’s below freezing out here! Annie arrives at Charlie, not seeing the distant torches. She seizes Charlie’s arm and st…\nANNIE: Are you an idiot? You can’t just roam around - no coat, no boots! Charlie YANKS her arm away from Annie.\nANNIE: Oh - what? You’re angry with me? Annie GRABS Charlie’s arm and PULLS her back toward the house.",
      "ANNIE: Hi.\nJOAN: Are you doing any better?\nANNIE: What?\nJOAN: With your mother...?",
      "JOAN: Annie! You came!\nANNIE JOAN: It’s a little earlier than we said. Ah, you’re perfect. Come in."
